Sources for `writing-plans` skill (see plans/skill-audits/writing-plans.md for full audit):

- superpowers/writing-plans — primary source. Used to ship Phase A–C of this very harness.
- superpowers/executing-plans — KEEP EXTERNAL. Plans transition to it. No improvement vector identified.
- superpowers/subagent-driven-development — reference for parallelizable plans.
- citypaul plan templates — sectioning style, numbered steps with verification gates.
- harness:plan-review — composed for high-risk plans (post-write review via CEO/Eng/Design/DevEx lenses; was gstack /autoplan, vendored in DEV-385).
- gstack /spec — VENDORED (DEV-388, the planning half): the executability gate (an unfamiliar implementer/agent could execute with zero follow-up questions) + MVP-cut-first. The precision/grounding half went to brainstorming.

Strategy: distill. Three deliberate changes from superpowers:
1. TDD mode per step (declared inline)
2. Resume point is first-class (every plan has one)
3. Verification gates between steps map explicitly to hooks

No companion hooks; the discipline is in the plan structure + downstream composition.
